<title>UK: Telemetrix sells U.S. Network Access business.</title>
<headline>Telemetrix sells U.S. Network Access business.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British telecommunications industry supplier Telemetrix Plc said on Wednesday that Promptus Communications Inc, owned by Telemetrix's U.S. unit GTI Corporation, had agreed to sell its Network Access Card business for around $20 million to Videoserver Inc.</p>
<p>The Network Access Card develops, markets and sells network access technology to enable access to high-speed digital network service, Telemetrix said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
